  "question": {
    "text": "Complete combustion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>750</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of an organic compound provides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>420</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>210</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>. The percentage composition of carbon and hydrogen in organic compound is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and ______ respectively. (Round off to the Nearest Integer)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>44</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi></math> carbon</p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>420</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>44</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>420</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1260</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mi>gm</mi></math> carbon</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>114</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>545</mn></math> gram carbon</p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math> of carbon <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>114</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>545</mn></mrow><mn>750</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8771;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>210</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>210</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>23</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>33</mn></mrow><mn>750</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>"
  }
